  "worked_solution": "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{3}{7}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{3}{7}=\\frac{(1\\times 7)+3}{7}=\\frac{10}{7}\n$$\n\nWe also write $6$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n6=\\frac{6}{1}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{7}\\times \\frac{6}{1}=\\frac{10\\times 6}{7\\times 1}=\\frac{60}{7}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $60.$",
